info.description:
nuMoni <strong>Orchestration + Frontend BFF</strong> — policy broadcast for every MS, plus the <code>/v1</code> entry the product Frontend uses.
Full client guide: <code>GET /frontend/integration-guide</code> (v1.7.0) · repo <code>FRONTEND_GATEWAY.md</code> · <code>USER_JOURNEYS.md</code>.

<p class="numoni-openapi-link"><strong>OpenAPI JSON:</strong> <a href="/docs/swagger.json" target="_blank" rel="noopener">/docs/swagger.json</a></p>
<div class="numoni-auth-callout"><strong>Frontend: use this Gateway only</strong> — Auth onboarding, money-core (Wallet / Point), Rewards, Card, Compliance (KYC), Create-App <em>and</em> Marketplace are proxied here. Filter Swagger: <code>Authentication</code>, <code>Wallet</code>, <code>Point</code>, <code>Reward</code>, <code>Card</code>, <code>Compliance</code>, <code>Create-App</code>, <code>Marketplace</code>.</div>
<p class="numoni-openapi-link"><strong>Machine-readable guide:</strong> <a href="/frontend/integration-guide" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GET /frontend/integration-guide</a> (v1.7.0) — Frontend uses <strong>only this Gateway</strong> for Auth + money-core (Wallet/Point) + Rewards (campaigns).</p>
<details class="numoni-api-overview" open><summary>Frontend onboarding — full POST bodies by user type</summary>
<p><strong>Base URL</strong> — set <code>NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL</code> to <code>http://localhost:8000/v1</code> (Kong) or <code>https://numoni-gateway-ms.fly.dev</code> (Fly BFF). NEXT_PUBLIC_API_MOCKING=disabled.</p>
<p><strong>Session</strong> — store fat JWT in <code>numoni_session</code>; send <code>Authorization: Bearer <accessToken></code>. Tokens from: <code>POST /journey/signup/verify</code>, <code>POST /journey/login</code>, <code>POST /journey/profile/* · /journey/pin</code>.</p>
<p><strong>OTP</strong> — Auth → notifications-ms (SMS always; email when address present). Mailtrap = email; Twilio / SMS_DEV_MODE = SMS. When OTP_DEV_MODE=true (Auth Fly default), responses include devOtp — use it in Swagger/FE without real SMS. Resend: <code>POST /journey/signup/otp { phone }</code>.</p>
<p><strong>Phone format</strong> — accepted: <code>+2348012345678</code>, <code>2348012345678</code>, <code>08012345678</code>, <code>8012345678</code>, <code>+234 (0) 801 234 5678</code>, <code>0801-234-5678</code>. Spaces, hyphens, dots and brackets are ignored. Nigerian numbers must be 234 + 7/8/9 + 9 digits. Other countries: full international number starting with + or 00. Auth stores and returns E.164 (+2348012345678). Login accepts any accepted format; send the same value in both login steps. <strong>One phone number per account across all user types (unique index on the account phone). Profile phone fields must equal the account phone.</strong> Errors: 400 "phone must be a valid phone number…" — format not accepted; 409 "Account already exists with this phone" — number already used by any account; 400 "phone must match the account phone number…" — profile phone differs from the account phone.</p>
<p><strong>Try-it-out</strong> — open <code>Authentication - Journey</code> → <code>POST /journey/signup</code> → Examples dropdown (Customer / SME / Fintech / Brand / Reseller).</p>
<p><strong>Route the UI on <code>nextStep</code></strong> (from signup/verify/login/me/profile/pin responses):</p>
<table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:0.9em"><thead><tr><th align="left">nextStep</th><th align="left">Meaning</th><th align="left">FE action</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>OTP</code></td><td>Signup OTP challenge outstanding</td><td>Show OTP screen; then POST /journey/signup/verify</td></tr><tr><td><code>LOGIN_OTP</code></td><td>Passwordless login OTP outstanding</td><td>Show OTP; resubmit POST /journey/login with phone + code</td></tr><tr><td><code>NAME</code></td><td>Customer needs display name (T1 done)</td><td>Name form → POST /journey/profile/customer</td></tr><tr><td><code>PIN</code></td><td>Customer name set; needs app PIN</td><td>PIN form → POST /journey/pin</td></tr><tr><td><code>PROFILE</code></td><td>Merchant/reseller missing businessName</td><td>Business profile → POST /journey/profile/business</td></tr><tr><td><code>DASHBOARD</code></td><td>Onboarding complete for this persona path</td><td>Enter workspace; optionally POST /policies/sync</td></tr></tbody></table>
<details class="numoni-api-overview" open><summary>Onboarding · Customer — <code>CUSTOMER</code></summary><p>phone → OTP → verify (T1 + token) → name → PIN → dashboard. Email optional at signup (profile quest later).</p><p><em>FE workspace:</em> /app (consumer)</p><p>Full POST bodies below — also available as named examples on <code>Authentication - Journey</code> Try-it-out.</p><ol><li><strong>1. Signup phone</strong> — <code>POST /journey/signup</code> (public)<br/>Optional: name, firstName, lastName, email, referralCode (links to merchant). Returns nextStep OTP + optional devOtp.<pre class="numoni-post-json">{
  "userType": "CUSTOMER",
  "phone": "08012345678",
  "referralCode": "NUM-A1B2C3"
}</pre></li><li><strong>2. OTP (optional resend)</strong> — <code>POST /journey/signup/otp</code> (public)<br/>Resend only. Skip if first signup response already has the code.<pre class="numoni-post-json">{
  "phone": "08012345678"
}</pre></li><li><strong>3. Verify OTP</strong> — <code>POST /journey/signup/verify</code> (public)<br/>Sets KYC T1. Store accessToken. nextStep is NAME (or PIN if name already set).<pre class="numoni-post-json">{
  "phone": "08012345678",
  "code": "123456",
  "purpose": "signup"
}</pre></li><li><strong>4. Name</strong> — <code>POST /journey/profile/customer</code> (bearer)<br/>Soft profile/quests: email, gender, ageGroup, work, salary, preferences, address, lat/lng, referralCode anytime.<pre class="numoni-post-json">{
  "universalId": "replace-with-JWT-userID",
  "firstName": "Ada",
  "lastName": "Okafor",
  "name": "Ada Okafor"
}</pre></li><li><strong>5. Create PIN</strong> — <code>POST /journey/pin</code> (bearer)<br/>4–6 digit PIN. nextStep DASHBOARD. Lock later: POST /journey/pin/verify, PATCH /journey/lock.<pre class="numoni-post-json">{
  "universalId": "replace-with-JWT-userID",
  "pin": "1234",
  "biometricEnabled": true
}</pre></li><li><strong>6. Returning login</strong> — <code>POST /journey/login</code> (public)<br/>First call may return requiresOtp + LOGIN_OTP (+ devOtp). Resubmit with phone + code → accessToken + nextStep.<pre class="numoni-post-json">{
  "phone": "08012345678"
}</pre></li></ol><p><strong>After dashboard</strong></p><ul><li>GET /journey/me — resume routing from nextStep</li><li>T2: Compliance (NIN/BVN + selfie) → POST /journey/kyc/tier2 or /kyc/compliance-result</li><li>T3: Compliance (statement + address) → POST /journey/kyc/tier3</li><li>POST /policies/sync — fan-out limits/permissions to MS</li><li>GET /consumer/account → workspace adapter (empty seed until Wallet/Point)</li></ul></details>
<details class="numoni-api-overview" open><summary>Onboarding · SME Merchant — <code>SME_MERCHANT</code></summary><p>businessName + phone + email → OTP → verify (T1) → usually DASHBOARD. Soft settings via business profile.</p><p><em>FE workspace:</em> /merchant</p><p>Full POST bodies below — also available as named examples on <code>Authentication - Journey</code> Try-it-out.</p><ol><li><strong>1. SME signup</strong> — <code>POST /journey/signup</code> (public)<br/>email + businessName required. referralCode → owning reseller. In Swagger Try-it-out pick example “2 · SME Merchant”.<pre class="numoni-post-json">{
  "userType": "SME_MERCHANT",
  "businessName": "Charles Store",
  "phone": "08012345678",
  "email": "charles@charlesstore.ng",
  "referralCode": "NUM-RESELLER"
}</pre></li><li><strong>2. Verify OTP</strong> — <code>POST /journey/signup/verify</code> (public)<br/>T1 + accessToken. With businessName at signup → nextStep DASHBOARD; else PROFILE.<pre class="numoni-post-json">{
  "phone": "08012345678",
  "code": "123456",
  "purpose": "signup"
}</pre></li><li><strong>3. Business profile (soft)</strong> — <code>POST /journey/profile/business</code> (bearer)<br/>Optional anytime. Required path if nextStep is PROFILE.<pre class="numoni-post-json">{
  "universalId": "replace-with-JWT-userID",
  "businessName": "Charles Store",
  "whatYouDo": "retail",
  "industry": "retail",
  "address": "24 Aminu Kano Crescent, Wuse II",
  "location": "abuja",
  "state": "Abuja",
  "city": "Wuse II",
  "latitude": 9.0765,
  "longitude": 7.3986,
  "rc": "RC1234567"
}</pre></li><li><strong>4. Login</strong> — <code>POST /journey/login</code> (public)<br/>First call may return requiresOtp; resubmit with code.<pre class="numoni-post-json">{
  "phone": "08012345678"
}</pre></li></ol><p><strong>After dashboard</strong></p><ul><li>T2: CAC (rc) + BVN via Compliance → POST /journey/kyc/tier2</li><li>T3: director ID + proof of address → /journey/kyc/tier3</li><li>POST /media/upload — KYC selfie/docs → CDN URL only in Mongo</li><li>GET /merchant/workspace → workspace adapter (empty seed until Reward OS data)</li></ul></details>
<details class="numoni-api-overview" open><summary>Onboarding · Fintech Merchant — <code>FINTECH_MERCHANT</code></summary><p>Same onboarding as SME; SK/PK issued when Tier 2 identity applies.</p><p><em>FE workspace:</em> /merchant</p><p>Full POST bodies below — also available as named examples on <code>Authentication - Journey</code> Try-it-out.</p><ol><li><strong>1. Fintech signup</strong> — <code>POST /journey/signup</code> (public)<br/>Swagger example “3 · Fintech Merchant”.<pre class="numoni-post-json">{
  "userType": "FINTECH_MERCHANT",
  "businessName": "PayLite NG",
  "phone": "08023456789",
  "email": "ops@paylite.ng",
  "referralCode": "NUM-RESELLER"
}</pre></li><li><strong>2. Verify OTP</strong> — <code>POST /journey/signup/verify</code> (public)<br/>Store accessToken; nextStep DASHBOARD or PROFILE.<pre class="numoni-post-json">{
  "phone": "08023456789",
  "code": "123456",
  "purpose": "signup"
}</pre></li><li><strong>3. Business profile</strong> — <code>POST /journey/profile/business</code> (bearer)<br/>Soft settings; required if nextStep is PROFILE.<pre class="numoni-post-json">{
  "universalId": "replace-with-JWT-userID",
  "businessName": "PayLite NG",
  "whatYouDo": "fintech",
  "industry": "payments",
  "email": "ops@paylite.ng",
  "phone": "08023456789",
  "website": "https://paylite.ng",
  "rc": "RC7654321"
}</pre></li></ol><p><strong>After dashboard</strong></p><ul><li>T2 → POST /journey/kyc/tier2 — Fintech SK/PK via /credentials/enterprise/*</li><li>T3 → POST /journey/kyc/tier3</li><li>GET /merchant/workspace → workspace adapter (empty seed until Reward OS data)</li></ul></details>
<details class="numoni-api-overview" open><summary>Onboarding · Brand Merchant — <code>BRAND_MERCHANT</code></summary><p>Brand / FMCG merchant — same signup contract as SME.</p><p><em>FE workspace:</em> /brand</p><p>Full POST bodies below — also available as named examples on <code>Authentication - Journey</code> Try-it-out.</p><ol><li><strong>1. Brand signup</strong> — <code>POST /journey/signup</code> (public)<br/>Swagger example “4 · Brand Merchant”.<pre class="numoni-post-json">{
  "userType": "BRAND_MERCHANT",
  "businessName": "Sunrise Beverages",
  "phone": "08034567890",
  "email": "trade@sunrise.ng",
  "referralCode": "NUM-RESELLER"
}</pre></li><li><strong>2. Verify OTP</strong> — <code>POST /journey/signup/verify</code> (public)<br/>Store accessToken.<pre class="numoni-post-json">{
  "phone": "08034567890",
  "code": "123456",
  "purpose": "signup"
}</pre></li></ol><p><strong>After dashboard</strong></p><ul><li>T2/T3 via Compliance handoff + /journey/kyc/*</li><li>GET /brand/workspace → workspace adapter (empty seed until brand/reward data)</li></ul></details>
<details class="numoni-api-overview" open><summary>Onboarding · Reseller — <code>RESELLER</code></summary><p>Same signup shape as merchants (businessName + phone + email → OTP → T1 → dashboard). Owns merchants via referral codes.</p><p><em>FE workspace:</em> /reseller</p><p>Full POST bodies below — also available as named examples on <code>Authentication - Journey</code> Try-it-out.</p><ol><li><strong>1. Reseller signup</strong> — <code>POST /journey/signup</code> (public)<br/>Swagger example “5 · Reseller”. Soft profile via /journey/profile/business.<pre class="numoni-post-json">{
  "userType": "RESELLER",
  "businessName": "Lagos Channel Partners",
  "phone": "08098765432",
  "email": "ops@lagoschannel.ng"
}</pre></li><li><strong>2. Verify OTP</strong> — <code>POST /journey/signup/verify</code> (public)<br/>Store accessToken; route on nextStep (DASHBOARD or PROFILE).<pre class="numoni-post-json">{
  "phone": "08098765432",
  "code": "123456",
  "purpose": "signup"
}</pre></li><li><strong>3. Business profile</strong> — <code>POST /journey/profile/business</code> (bearer)<br/>Optional soft profile.<pre class="numoni-post-json">{
  "universalId": "replace-with-JWT-userID",
  "businessName": "Lagos Channel Partners",
  "whatYouDo": "distribution",
  "email": "ops@lagoschannel.ng",
  "phone": "08098765432",
  "address": "Ikeja, Lagos"
}</pre></li></ol><p><strong>After dashboard</strong></p><ul><li>Share referralCode with merchants at their signup</li><li>GET /reseller/workspace → workspace adapter (empty seed until reseller org data)</li></ul></details>
<details class="numoni-api-overview" open><summary>Onboarding · Platform Admin</summary><p>Not public signup. Bootstrap once via Gateway, then invite. Login via /journey/login. Full bodies in Authentication - Platform Admin Try-it-out.</p><ol><li><strong>1. First Platform Owner (ops only)</strong> — <code>POST /admin/bootstrap</code> (public)<br/>One-time. Use Gateway Try-it-out — no Auth Swagger needed.<pre class="numoni-post-json">{
  "bootstrapSecret": "replace-with-PLATFORM_ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_SECRET",
  "firstName": "Platform",
  "lastName": "Owner",
  "email": "owner@numoni.ng",
  "phone": "08000000001"
}</pre></li><li><strong>2. Invite another admin</strong> — <code>POST /admin/invite</code> (bearer)<br/>Bearer Platform Owner. Invitee completes phone OTP.<pre class="numoni-post-json">{
  "firstName": "Ops",
  "lastName": "Lead",
  "email": "ops@numoni.ng",
  "phone": "08000000002",
  "role": "admin"
}</pre></li><li><strong>3. Admin login</strong> — <code>POST /journey/login</code> (public)<br/>OTP → accessToken. FE GET /admin/overview is analytics adapter ≠ Auth /admin/users.<pre class="numoni-post-json">{
  "phone": "08000000001"
}</pre></li></ol></details>
<p><strong>Policies</strong> — After login/KYC changes, sync policy so Wallet/Point/etc. see limits without chatty Auth calls. <code>POST /policies/sync</code> · <code>GET /policies/me</code></p>
<p><strong>Workspace adapters</strong> — Bearer workspace GETs aggregate Reward (campaigns/prizes), Card (inventory), Marketplace (storefronts). Analytics charts derive from Reward/Card when ANALYTICS_MS_URL unset. Wallet balance soft-hydrates when WALLET_MS_URL is set; full money APIs are under /wallet/* and /points/*; campaign APIs are under /rewards/*. Examples: <code>/merchant/workspace</code> · <code>/merchant/analytics</code> · <code>/consumer/account</code> · <code>/admin/overview</code> · <code>/reseller/workspace</code> · <code>/brand/workspace</code> · <code>/enterprise/workspace</code> · <code>/brand-app/account</code> · <code>/till/workspace</code>. Response: <code>{ success, message, data }</code>.</p>
<p><strong>501 stubs</strong> — Remaining FE paths still return 501 FeNotImplementedDto until org adapters exist. <code>/orgs/:orgId/settings</code> · <code>/orgs/:orgId/compliance</code>. Meta: <code>GET /access-map · GET /frontend/integration-guide</code>.</p>
</details>
<details class="numoni-api-overview" open><summary>Money core + Rewards — Wallet, Point, Reward (via Gateway)</summary>
<p>Closed-loop money + reward APIs are proxied on this Gateway. Prefer these over calling Wallet/Point/Reward Fly URLs directly from the Frontend. Reward MS has no /v1 prefix: /rewards/campaigns -&gt; Reward MS /campaigns.</p>
<p><strong>Prefixes</strong> — Wallet <code>/wallet/*</code> → Wallet MS <code>/v1/*</code>; Point <code>/points/*</code> → Point MS <code>/v1/*</code>; Rewards <code>/rewards/*</code> → Reward MS <code>/*</code> (no /v1).</p>
<p><strong>Headers</strong> — <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;accessToken&gt;</code> · <code>Idempotency-Key: &lt;unique per money mutation&gt;</code> · <code>Content-Type: application/json</code> · <code>X-Correlation-ID: &lt;optional uuid&gt;</code></p>
<ul><li><strong>Company funds Buy Pool (mint)</strong><ol><li><code>ADMIN JWT → POST /points/opt-in (once)</code></li><li><code>POST /points/admin/mint { fiatAmount, currency, pointsToMint, rate, fundingSource } + Idempotency-Key</code></li><li><code>GET /points/admin/pools to confirm BUY_POOL / totalMinted</code></li></ol></li><li><strong>Customer / merchant buy points (PayOnUs VA)</strong><ol><li><code>POST /wallet/opt-in</code></li><li><code>POST /wallet/wallets { currency: NGN }</code></li><li><code>POST /wallet/wallets/{walletId}/buy-points { points, name, email, phone } + Idempotency-Key</code></li><li><code>Show payment.accountNumber / bankName; poll POST /wallet/buy-orders/{id}/verify-payment or wait for webhook</code></li><li><code>GET /wallet/wallets/{walletId} → balance</code></li></ol></li><li><strong>P2P / QR spend</strong><ol><li><code>POST /wallet/transfers { fromWalletId, toWalletId, points } + Idempotency-Key</code></li><li><code>or POST /wallet/qr/generate then POST /wallet/qr/confirm</code></li></ol></li><li><strong>Redeem → Sell Pool → fiat settlement</strong><ol><li><code>POST /wallet/wallets/{walletId}/redeem { points } + Idempotency-Key</code></li><li><code>Optional POST /wallet/payouts/name-enquiry { accountNumber, bankCode }</code></li><li><code>POST /wallet/wallets/{walletId}/settlements { points, accountNumber, bankCode, email, accountName? } + Idempotency-Key (PayOnUs min ₦500)</code></li><li><code>On payout fail, Gateway/Wallet auto reverse-settles Sell Pool (no FE compensate needed unless settle_reverse_failed recon)</code></li></ol></li><li><strong>Merchant / enterprise campaign wizard (Reward MS)</strong><ol><li><code>POST /rewards/opt-in (once per user)</code></li><li><code>GET /rewards/enums to load rule types, prize types, channels, statuses</code></li><li><code>POST /rewards/campaigns (step 1: name, description, channel, dates) -&gt; campaignId</code></li><li><code>PATCH /rewards/campaigns/{campaignId}/audience-channels (step 2)</code></li><li><code>POST /rewards/campaigns/{campaignId}/rewards or PUT .../rewards for bulk (step 3)</code></li><li><code>PATCH /rewards/campaigns/{campaignId}/budget (step 4: locks escrow)</code></li><li><code>POST /rewards/campaigns/{campaignId}/start (step 5: ACTIVE or SCHEDULED)</code></li><li><code>GET /rewards/campaigns for the list + KPIs; POST .../pause | resume | stop (stop releases unspent escrow)</code></li></ol></li></ul>
<p><strong>Do not call from FE</strong> — Wallet PayOnUs webhook URL (server-to-server only); Point /v1/internal/* (service key; Wallet MS only); Direct Fly wallet-ms / points-ms / reward-ms from browser when Gateway is available; POST /rewards/campaigns/evaluate and /rewards/campaigns/evaluations/{ref}/reverse are for checkout/orchestration services, not the FE.</p>
<p><strong>Swagger filter</strong> — <code>Wallet</code>, <code>Point</code> or <code>Reward</code> for Try-it-out DTOs.</p>
</details>
<details class="numoni-api-overview" open><summary>Other services via Gateway — Card · Compliance · Create-App · Marketplace</summary><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:0.9em"><thead><tr><th align="left">Prefix</th><th align="left">Maps to</th><th align="left">Use</th><th align="left">Not exposed</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>/card/*</code></td><td>/* (e.g. /card/cards/my -&gt; /cards/my)</td><td>Reward cards: list/my, activate, unlock (initiate/verify), charge, ledger, status, enums</td><td>callbacks/*, cards/webhooks/*, health, docs</td></tr><tr><td><code>/compliance/*</code></td><td>/api/v1/* (e.g. /compliance/kyc/status/{userId} -&gt; /api/v1/kyc/status/{userId}); /compliance/opt-in -&gt; /opt-in</td><td>KYC: individual + business submit/status/documents, shareholders + liveness link, admin review queue</td><td>kyc/liveness/webhook (provider callback), health, docs</td></tr><tr><td><code>/create-app/*</code></td><td>/api/v1/apps/* (e.g. /create-app/apps -&gt; /api/v1/apps); /create-app/opt-in -&gt; /opt-in</td><td>White-label apps: create, submit, approve/reject, product keys, transactions, drive documents</td><td>special/* (API-key partner API), health, docs</td></tr><tr><td><code>/marketplace/*</code></td><td>/api/v1/* (e.g. /marketplace/merchant/stores -&gt; /api/v1/merchant/stores)</td><td>Stores, products, cart, orders, reviews, storefront by slug, admin dashboard. Product image upload (multipart) is supported</td><td>internal/* (service key), health, docs</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Same Bearer fat JWT everywhere. Notifications MS is not proxied (service-key OTP sender used by Auth).</p></details>
<p><strong>Errors</strong> — <strong>400</strong> Validation / bad journey state / insufficient funds; <strong>401</strong> Missing/invalid JWT or OTP/PIN; <strong>403</strong> Wrong user / non-admin; <strong>404</strong> Unknown user/resource; <strong>409</strong> Duplicate phone/email / idempotency conflict; <strong>501</strong> FE org stub (settings/compliance) — not Auth; <strong>502</strong> Auth / Wallet / Point / Reward / Card / Compliance / Create-App / Marketplace MS unreachable from BFF proxy; <strong>503</strong> A *_MS_URL (WALLET, POINT, REWARD, CARD, COMPLIANCE, CREATE_APP, MARKETPLACE) is unset on gateway.</p>
<details class="numoni-api-overview"><summary>Gateway plumbing (proxy · policies · stubs)</summary>
<p><strong>Auth (proxied)</strong> — <code>POST /journey/signup|login|…</code>, profiles, credentials, media, and Auth platform-admin routes → Authentication MS.</p>
<p><strong>Wallet (proxied)</strong> — <code>/wallet/*</code> → Wallet MS <code>/v1/*</code> (buy-points, redeem, settlements, transfers, QR, admin recon). PayOnUs webhooks stay on Wallet MS directly.</p>
<p><strong>Point (proxied)</strong> — <code>/points/*</code> → Point MS <code>/v1/*</code> (opt-in, <code>POST /points/admin/mint</code> company Buy Pool funding, pools, recon). Internal SAM routes are <em>not</em> exposed.</p>
<p><strong>Reward (proxied)</strong> — <code>/rewards/*</code> → Reward MS <code>/*</code> (campaign wizard, rewards, budget, start/pause/stop, evaluate, ledger, enums, admin guardrails). Reward MS health and Swagger are <em>not</em> exposed.</p>
<p><strong>Card (proxied)</strong> — <code>/card/*</code> → Card MS <code>/*</code> (cards, activate, unlock, charge, ledger, enums). Policy callbacks and the ledger webhook are <em>not</em> exposed.</p>
<p><strong>Compliance (proxied)</strong> — <code>/compliance/*</code> → Compliance MS <code>/api/v1/*</code> (individual + business KYC, admin review). The liveness provider webhook is <em>not</em> exposed.</p>
<p><strong>Create-App (proxied)</strong> — <code>/create-app/apps/*</code> → Create-App MS <code>/api/v1/apps/*</code> (white-label apps, product keys, drive). The API-key <code>/special/*</code> partner API is <em>not</em> exposed.</p>
<p><strong>Marketplace (proxied)</strong> — <code>/marketplace/*</code> → Marketplace MS <code>/api/v1/*</code> (stores, products, cart, orders, storefront, admin). <code>/internal/*</code> is <em>not</em> exposed.</p>
<p><strong>Policies</strong> — after login/KYC, <code>POST /policies/sync</code> or <code>GET /policies/me</code>.</p>
<p><strong>FE workspaces</strong> — Bearer workspace adapters; meta <code>GET /access-map</code>.</p>
<p><strong>Bearer</strong> — fat JWT <code>accessToken</code> (claim <code>userID</code>). Shared <code>JWT_SECRET</code>. Money mutating routes also need <code>Idempotency-Key</code>.</p>
</details>
